# Six berths of six are taken and a seventh berth's worth has nowhere to stand.
#
# **No rule mentions berths.** `move` puts the scout down and the world it would leave consumes
# seven where six are provided, which is where the refusal comes from - so this binds every rule
# that puts a vehicle anywhere, including ones not written yet.

{test name:a-scout-cannot-move-where-every-berth-is-taken}

{given}
{provides kind:territory what:berth} -> 6
{consumes kind:scout what:berth} -> 1
{consumes kind:transport what:berth} -> 2
{territory id:1 name:territory-1}
{territory id:2 name:territory-2}
{adjacency id:1 from:territory-1 to:territory-2}
{scout where:territory-1 moving:1} -> 1
{transport where:territory-2 moving:1} -> 3

{when}
{move what:scout from:territory-1 to:territory-2}

{refused}
{provides kind:territory what:berth} -> 7
